hey welcome everybody um one of the  things we're going to spend some time  talking about today are the recent  protests  and unrest and violence and the way that  uh people have been trying to take  advantage of that violence and unrest  but before we even do that one of the  things i want to talk about is this  broader context  in which donald trump is running for  president  as if someone else has been president  for the last  four years and that's just one  aspect of what i want to focus in on  today and and that particular aspect is  really unlike anything we've seen  um in the modern political era for  presidents running for re-election most  presidents have run for re-election  very clearly on i've been in charge for  four years  and we're going to get another four  years that will be similar to the last  four  and that's good donald trump is doing  something very very different and that's  what i want to talk about now before we  get we get into that i guess it's  important to mention  i'm leaving a lot out of this analysis  uh  in terms of things that donald trump is  doing of course this has been one of the  most dishonest presidencies the lie  count is off the charts and donald trump  has been doing a lot of lying  to justify his re-election as well okay  on the  issues donald trump has failed to  deliver on a bunch of different campaign  issues  the wall replacing the health care  system on and on and on  but there's a reason that i want to  focus in on this particular aspect  because it relates to  the sort of gaslighty nature  of the campaign as well as the  um intellectually compromised element of  donald trump's electorate  which is that donald trump is framing  his re-election campaign as if you need  to choose him  instead of what we've had for the last  four years and unfortunately it's  working on a lot of people as evidenced  by some of the interviews when you go to  these rallies that donald trump has been  doing  the rnc etc and the language that trump  is using suggests somebody else has  been in charge for the last four years  and in order to  fix that donald trump must be elected  when you look at this phrase make  america great again  again that is predicated  on the implicit understanding that trump  won in 2016 and for a while he was great  and he made america great again  and then that sort of fell apart  including with coronavirus  and the economy and now we need to elect  trump in order to make america great  again again because it's almost like  trump hasn't been the one in charge for  the last six or seven months  we have to put trump back in power to  fix problems  that were actually created during donald  trump's presidency  as if he was not in charge during that  time this  is going to be a big factor in our  discussion about  protests and unrest donald trump  has been talking about the mass protests  and the unrest  with the framing of democrat cities as  he says  run by far-left mayors anarchists or  anarchists  as he calls them marxists and others the  reality  is that it's trump himself who has  generated the unrest  we didn't have unrest like this when joe  biden was vice president for eight years  and i'm going to come back to that in a  little bit  there's been donald trump's mishandling  of so many issues  but trump is running as if other people  have been in charge for the last six  months  and in order to get things back under  control  you need to elect donald trump now of  course any thinking person would realize  trump is saying things are out of  control with me as president  so re-elect me to fix it but  of course why would we do that why  wouldn't trump  just be able to get things under control  now in other words why is he  saying that only in his second term will  he be able to get these things under  control and of course when you realize  that he's been what's been generating  the unrest and the discontent  the entire argument falls apart in in  some sense  trump is almost running against himself  but  putting in joe biden as a proxy to take  the hit  for donald trump's own failings and i i  wish it weren't  the case there's really no way to say  this without offending some people  but his supporters that are eating it up  are eating it up in great part because  they are intellectually compromised now  some of them know it's bs  but they want trump re-elected for other  reasons and so they're just jumping on  the bandwagon but a lot of people are  actually falling for this stuff  now there's a few different thoughts  about why donald trump  is doing this one thought is that this  is some kind of four-dimensional chess  he's taking credit for successes but  painting the failings on joe biden or on  democratic mayors or whoever the case  may be and it's all  kind of uh calculated to paint him  as the underdog despite the fact that  he's the incumbent right we could go  into some kind of more complex  analysis the other explanation is way  simpler which is trump's a one-trick  pony  he doesn't know how to run as the  incumbent  and he is running the exact same  campaign  that he ran as the supposed political  outsider in 2016  he's just running the same campaign  ignoring the fact that he's been the  president for four years  we really have not seen anything like  this and it's preying upon  the most ignorant voters but that is not  a guarantee that it's going to fail to  work it very well  could succeed and this is why i've been  sounding the alarm now for several weeks  saying  we can't write off what to many of us  seem like  obviously terrible strategies as  ineffective  because it may work donald trump  genuinely expects that americans are  going to fall for this  and plenty of americans are falling for  it now  the other thing on top of this which we  have to remember  is that joe biden was sort of in charge  for eight years in other words when joe  biden was vice president  okay barack obama was the president but  we didn't have in obama and biden's  america  chaos and unrest the likes of which  donald trump is now preemptively  assigning to joe biden you had tea  partiers  who sometimes protested uh you you had  ferguson which was a  very different thing than what we have  going on right now you certainly had  shootings but that was a gun problem  which we have not fixed  but things were actually far more calm  during the era  in which joe biden was vice president to  the president of the united states  and so at even on the facts  you don't even have to hypothesize what  it would be like  if joe biden were president you can go  back and see what things were like when  joe biden was vice president and we're  going to get  into later on in the program why  is it that trump benefits from chaos  and unrest you would think that if  people  were thinking clearly they would say oh  if there's chaos and unrest  while trump is president doesn't make  sense to vote for him again  to fix it we should vote for someone  else that would be a logical assessment  i'm going to explain to you later on in  the program  uh why why that doesn't work or in other  words why  donald trump does benefit from the chaos  and why he's trying to incite it but  before we go to that let's talk about  the after effects of the republican  national convention
 

